### VS Code REST Client Requests for FastAPI User Endpoints

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1

# Define a variable to store the access token after login
# You will copy the token from the login response and paste it here
@accessToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhbGljZUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInVzZXJfaWQiOjEsImV4cCI6MTc1MTM1ODc0M30.5I4vhElItvzVVBqEltigks6hj9iGs5tW-GenQpQRzwg
### 1. Create a New User (POST /api/v1/users/)
# This endpoint does not require authentication.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "alice@example.com",
    "password": "StrongPassword123",
    "password_confirm": "StrongPassword123",
    "name": "Test User",
    "schrittlaenge": 0.75
}

### 2. User Login (POST /api/v1/auth/login)
# Replace with your actual auth login endpoint and credentials.
# The response will contain the access_token. Copy it and paste it into @accessToken variable above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "alice@example.com",
    "password": "StrongPassword123"
}

### 3. Get All Users (GET /api/v1/users/)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3.1. Get All Team Members (GET /api/v1/team_members/)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.
# This endpoint is used to retrieve all team members.
GET {{baseUrl}}/team_members
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3.2. Get All Challenges (GET /api/v1/challenges/)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.
# This endpoint is used to retrieve all challenges
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3.3. Get All Teams (GET /api/v1/teams/)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.
# This endpoint is used to retrieve all teams.
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Get Current User (GET /api/v1/users/me)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.

### 3.4. Get All Teams (GET /api/v1/teams/)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.
# This endpoint is used to retrieve all teams.
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenge_progress
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Get Current User (GET /api/v1/users/me)
# Requires authentication using the obtained access token.


GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Get User by ID (GET /api/v1/users/{user_id})
# Replace {user_id} with an actual user ID (e.g., 1, 2, etc.).
# Requires authentication.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6. Update an Existing User (PUT /api/v1/users/{user_id})
# Replace {user_id} with the ID of the user you want to update.
# Requires authentication. Only the current user can update their own profile.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "full_name": "Updated Test User Name",
    "is_active": true
}

### 7. Delete an Existing User (DELETE /api/v1/users/{user_id})
# Replace {user_id} with the ID of the user you want to delete.
# Requires authentication. Only the current user can delete their own account.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 8. Update User Profile with Additional Fields
# This example updates the user's name and step length.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "name": "Jeton Arifia",
    "schrittlaenge": 0.80
}


